   $q$What did Hester Galloway and the farmers argue for?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Hiring a second ferry to run during the spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Building a wooden bridge across the Calder River.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Lowering the fee the ferry charged for wagons.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Moving the town of Fairhaven to the west side.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Building a wooden bridge across the Calder River.$q$, $q$The second paragraph says the farmers "asked the town council to build a wooden bridge." The ferry fee is one of their reasons, not their request.$q$, 'draft', '285b6af8-886f-5a81-bd52-7ac4b44c20fb')
