   $q$Which statement in the debate is an opinion given with no reason or evidence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The farmers' statement that the ferry stopped for nineteen days in April.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-support"},{"text":"Galloway's statement that her family paid the ferry over forty times.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-support"},{"text":"The builder's report that a bridge on stone piers could stand for years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-support"},{"text":"Wren's statement that the ferry has always been good enough for Fairhaven.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Wren's statement that the ferry has always been good enough for Fairhaven.$q$, $q$Saying something "has always been good enough" is not a reason or evidence, and the farmers had shown it was not good enough in April. Galloway's statement is backed by her ledger, and the builder's is backed by his study and drawings.$q$, 'draft', '285b6af8-886f-5a81-bd52-7ac4b44c20fb')
